        "normas.hero_title": "RULES",
        "normas.hero_subtitle": "Official Rules for all Mosco Events events",
        "normas.pdf_card_title": "Official Regulations",
        "normas.pdf_card_text": "Download the full Mosco Events rulebook in PDF format.",
        "normas.pdf_button": "DOWNLOAD PDF",
        "normas.section_heading": "OFFICIAL RULES",
        "normas.intro": "Mandatory for all participants. Registering for any event implies full acceptance of these rules.",
        "normas.index_title": "Go to section",
        "normas.index.seguridad": "1. Safety",
        "normas.index.replicas": "2. Replicas and equipment",
        "normas.index.juego": "3. Game rules",
        "normas.index.conducta": "4. Conduct and authority",
        "normas.index.disciplina": "5. Disciplinary rules",
        "normas.seguridad.p1": "<strong>1.1. Mandatory eye protection.</strong> From the moment you enter the playing field, wearing approved protective eyewear is mandatory at all times. Removing it outside the safe zones designated by the organization is strictly forbidden.",
        "normas.seguridad.p2": "<strong>1.2. Replicas in the bar and rest area.</strong> Carrying replicas in the bar or rest area is not allowed. All replicas must stay outside this area or comply with the safety instructions set by the organization.",
        "normas.seguridad.p3": "<strong>1.3. Field elements.</strong> It is forbidden to move, displace, remove or modify any field object that has not been expressly authorized or marked by the organization for that purpose.",
        "normas.replicas.p1": "<strong>2.1. Maximum power.</strong> The maximum authorized power is <strong>1.14 J</strong>. There is no BB weight limit.",
        "normas.replicas.p2": "<strong>2.2. Chronograph testing.</strong> The organization may require a chrono check at any time during the event, under the following conditions:",
        "normas.replicas.li1": "The replica will be chronographed with the BB and hop-up set exactly as they will be used in play.",
        "normas.replicas.li2": "Gas replicas must be presented for chrono testing with BBs, but <strong>without gas loaded in the magazine</strong>. Loading will be done in front of the organization, to verify that the replica does not exceed the limit with a fully loaded magazine.",
        "normas.replicas.p3": "<strong>2.3. Firing mode.</strong> Only semi-automatic firing is allowed. Full-auto mode, semi-ramping and binary mode are completely forbidden, as is modifying the electronic trigger via Bluetooth apps.",
        "normas.replicas.p4": "<strong>2.4. Magazines.</strong> The use of Hi-Cap magazines is not allowed.",
        "normas.replicas.p5": "<strong>2.5. Grenades.</strong> The use of grenades of any kind is not allowed during the event, unless expressly authorized by the organization.",
        "normas.juego.p1": "<strong>3.1. \"Lebanese-style\" blind fire.</strong> Firing blind (so-called \"Lebanese-style\"), i.e. shooting without exposing your head or having direct sight of the target, is not allowed under any circumstances.",
        "normas.juego.p2": "<strong>3.2. Firing through gaps.</strong> Firing through gaps or openings is not allowed if the replica's barrel is not <strong>1 m or more</strong> from the parapet. However, receiving hits through such gaps, however small, is valid.",
        "normas.juego.p3": "<strong>3.3. CQB zones.</strong> All CQB zones on the field are considered enclosed rooms. Therefore, firing over the walls or structures that enclose them is not allowed, and hits received that way will not be considered valid.",
        "normas.juego.p4": "<strong>3.4. Simultaneous engagements.</strong> When two players are facing each other, aiming at one another, and both fire at the same time, both will be considered eliminated. This rule only applies when both players are facing and aiming at each other; if one of them is not aiming at the other at that moment, the situation will be resolved according to the usual elimination rules.",
        "normas.conducta.p1": "<strong>4.1. Respect and sportsmanship.</strong> Absolute respect towards other participants, referees and organization members is required. Any unsportsmanlike conduct, insult, threat or lack of respect may result in immediate expulsion from the event.",
        "normas.conducta.p2": "<strong>4.2. Organization's decisions.</strong> The decisions of the organization and the referee team are mandatory throughout the event and are not open to discussion on the playing field.",
        "registro.signature_alt": "Participant's signature",
        "normas.disciplina.panel": "Anyone who breaches any of the rules in these regulations will be subject to the disciplinary measures the organization considers appropriate, depending on the severity of the infringement. Such measures may include warnings, sanctions, immediate expulsion from the event or, in the most serious or repeated cases, permanent expulsion from the field and a ban on taking part in future Mosco Events events."
